# C11 user-event read — DO NOT APPLY

Issue: https://github.com/liboyang42-cpu/chengyin-remote-ops/issues/5
Repo: github.com/liboyang42-cpu/hengyin
Base: origin/cursor/c11-ops-support-adapters-d6bd
Branch: cursor/c11-user-event-read-e504

DO NOT APPLY this hunk. Do not edit ApiRegistrationController.java, BusinessAuditLogController.java, BusinessAuditEventMapper.java, or BusinessAuditEventMapper.xml from this branch.

The method belongs beside POST /api/registration/info on ApiRegistrationController (`@RequestMapping("/api/registration")`). It does not belong on /business/audit-log. `/business/audit-log/list` stays admin-only. This addition does not call that list, does not add an admin role, and does not add a permission string.

The service `MemberOwnedOrderOriginalEventRead.readOwnedOrder` is already real. The controller only forwards the current member from `getAppUserId()` into that service. Mockito in the service test is in-memory. It is not HTTP and it is not MySQL.

